        <type>std::string</type>
        <definition>std::string Rose::AST::NodeId::run_hash</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>run_hash</name>
        <briefdescription>
<para><ref refid="classA" kindref="compound">A</ref> hash uniquely identifing the command line and ROSE version. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>NodeIDs are only stable if the same files are input and the same version of ROSE is used. (Well, there are probably other ways to screw it up, like building ROSE with different compilers) So this hash is to ensure that the input files and the ROSE version are the same when the <ref refid="classRose_1_1AST_1_1NodeId" kindref="compound">NodeId</ref> is read and written.</para><para>Dan would prefer that this hash was associated directly with the SgProject node, so, if one day we actually managed to have more than one SgProject node in the <ref refid="namespaceRose_1_1AST" kindref="compound">AST</ref>, this would be easier to adapt. But the problem is that would mean we&apos;d have to pass an SgNode to getNodeId(string) which would be possible, but weird. So I&apos;m going with this for now. 2023/03/15 </para>        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
